# Phanttom relaunch — Debug only, clean env

When rebuilding/relaunching a local Debug Ghostty/Phanttom build:

## Quit target

- **Only** quit `com.mitchellh.ghostty.debug` (the Debug build from `macos/build/Debug/Ghostty.app`).
- **Never** quit `com.mitchellh.ghostty` — that is the user's production Phanttom/Ghostty (e.g. `~/Applications/Phanttom.app`).
- **Never** `pkill -x ghostty`, `killall ghostty`, or any broad process kill that matches all Ghostty binaries. Prod and Debug share the process name `ghostty`.

## Launch environment (colors)

Cursor agent shells often set `NO_COLOR=1`, `FORCE_COLOR=0`, and `TERM=dumb`. Bare `open …/Ghostty.app` from that shell **inherits those into the Debug app**, and Claude Code / other TUIs render without color.

- **Always** relaunch via `macos/relaunch-debug.sh` (preferred), **or** the same `env -i … TERM=xterm-256color COLORTERM=truecolor /usr/bin/open …` pattern inside that script.
- **Never** plain `open macos/build/Debug/Ghostty.app` from an agent/CI shell.

```sh
# ✅ OK — Debug only, clean env
macos/relaunch-debug.sh

# ✅ OK — quit Debug only (script does this too)
osascript -e 'tell application id "com.mitchellh.ghostty.debug" to quit'

# ❌ NEVER — kills prod
osascript -e 'tell application id "com.mitchellh.ghostty" to quit'
pkill -x ghostty

# ❌ NEVER — strips TUI colors when run from Cursor agent shells
open macos/build/Debug/Ghostty.app
```

If Debug is not running, still use `macos/relaunch-debug.sh` (or the clean-env `open`). Leave any other Ghostty/Phanttom instance alone unless the user explicitly asks to quit it.
